msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:108
msgid "Verify delivery"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:109
msgid "This plugin is only worth anything if its alerts actually arrive. A rejected sender address fails silently on many hosts, so it is worth proving delivery once."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:112
msgid "Send a test alert"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:118
msgid "Choose what happens for each event. \"E-mail\" sends immediately and also writes to the log; \"Log only\" records it without sending; \"Off\" ignores the event entirely."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:138
#: admin/views/page-settings.php:284
msgid "Action"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:153
msgid "E-mail"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:154
msgid "Log only"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:155
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:178
msgid "PHP has no OpenSSL support on this server, so there is nowhere safe to keep a shared secret. Two-factor authentication stays off until that is fixed — storing the secret in the clear would make a database dump enough to bypass it."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:182
msgid "A one-time code from an authenticator app, asked for after the password is accepted. Enrolment is per account: every user manages their own from their profile."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:187
msgid "Availability"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:190
msgid "Let users protect their account with an authenticator app"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:191
msgid "Switching this off does not delete anything. Enrolled users simply stop being asked, and are asked again if it is switched back on."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:195
msgid "Administrators"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:198
msgid "Require it for everyone who can manage options"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:199
msgid "They are nagged during the grace period below, and cannot sign in without enrolling once it has passed. The clock starts when you save this, not when the plugin was installed."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:201
msgid "Grace period"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: formatted date
#: admin/views/page-settings.php:213
#, php-format
msgid "Enrolment becomes mandatory on %s."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:216
msgid "The grace period has passed. Administrators without a second factor must enrol at their next sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:224
msgid "Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:226
msgid "Ten single-use recovery codes are issued at enrolment and shown once. They are stored only as hashes, which is also why they survive a rotation of the site salts when the authenticator secrets do not."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:228
msgid "Also allow a one-time code sent to the account e-mail address"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:230
msgid "A real weakening: anyone who can read that mailbox can complete the sign-in, and on many sites the mailbox is on the same hosting account. Worth having when losing a phone would otherwise mean losing the site — not worth having otherwise. Every send and every use is logged."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:233
msgid "The mailed code expires after"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:236
#: admin/views/page-settings.php:383
msgid "minutes"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:238
msgid "If a user loses the authenticator, the recovery codes and the mailbox, any administrator can reset their second factor from that user's profile screen."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:242
msgid "Your account"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:248
msgid "Two-factor authentication is on for your account."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:249
msgid "Two-factor authentication is not set up for your account."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:253
msgid "Manage it"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:260
msgid "What is not covered"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:261
msgid "Application passwords, the REST API and XML-RPC are not challenged. There is nobody at the keyboard to type a code, and an application password is already a separate credential you can revoke on its own. If an account must be locked down completely, revoke its application passwords as well."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:275
#: admin/views/page-status.php:51
msgid "Location checks"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:279
msgid "Evaluate and log the country of every successful login"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:288
msgid "Monitor only — alert, but let the login through"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:292
msgid "Block logins from countries that are not on the list"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:295
msgid "Blocking cannot be armed: no working country lookup is available. Install a GeoIP database below, or configure a trusted CDN country header."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:297
msgid "Blocking cannot be armed while the country list is empty."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:300
msgid "An address whose country cannot be determined counts as not allowed and is blocked. VPN and Tor traffic usually falls into this category. If the lookup breaks entirely, blocking switches itself back to monitor mode rather than locking everyone out."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:305
#: admin/views/page-status.php:66
msgid "Allowed countries"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:309
msgid "Two-letter ISO country codes, separated by spaces. For example: CH DE AT"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: country name, 2: country code
#: admin/views/page-settings.php:315
#, php-format
msgid "You are currently connecting from %1$s (%2$s)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:325
msgid "Always-allowed addresses"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:328
msgid "One IP address or CIDR block per line, IPv4 or IPv6. These skip the country rule entirely. Private, loopback and link-local addresses are always allowed and need not be listed."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:332
msgid "Denied addresses"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:336
msgid "One IP address or CIDR block per line, IPv4 or IPv6. These can never sign in — the deny list is checked before everything else, so it overrides the allow list, an allowed country, and even the private-network exemption. It applies whether or not country checking is switched on."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:339
msgid "The check runs after the password has been verified, so the log records who tried and with which account — a blocked entry here means someone at that address had working credentials. It stops the login, not the traffic: for that, deny the address in your firewall or CDN, where it costs nothing to refuse."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the administrator's current IP address
#: admin/views/page-settings.php:345
#, php-format
msgid "Your current address is %s. An entry matching it is refused on save, so this list cannot lock you out of your own site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:353
#: admin/views/page-status.php:92
msgid "Trusted proxies"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:356
msgid "Forwarding headers such as X-Forwarded-For are read ONLY when the connecting address is in this list. Leave it empty if the site is not behind a proxy or CDN — trusting a header that anyone can send would let an attacker choose their own apparent location."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:359
msgid "Use the country header supplied by the CDN (CF-IPCountry) when available"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:364
msgid "API authentication"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:368
msgid "Apply location rules to application passwords and XML-RPC as well"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:370
msgid "Off by default. These authenticate through the same mechanism as an interactive login, so turning this on can silently break integrations whose servers sit abroad."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:374
msgid "Bypass link"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:378
msgid "E-mail a single-use recovery link whenever a login is blocked"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:381
msgid "Link valid for"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:386
msgid "grants access for"
